# Auditable allowlist for the secret scan step of scripts/gate.sh.
#
# One extended regex per line; each must be preceded by a comment saying who
# approved it and why, so this file is a record rather than a mute button.
#
# The house scanner's own pattern list (~/meta/scripts/secret-scan.sh) is NEVER
# edited to make a push go through. Anything new that hits stays a failure.
#
# Note the bracket trick ([x] instead of x): it keeps this file from tripping
# the very patterns it allows, since a regex still matches text written that
# way but a literal-string scan does not.

# Nick's call, 2026-10-24. wezterm.lua is published as a real working config,
# not a sanitized template. This is the RFC 1918 address in its ssh_domains
# block: home network, unreachable from the internet. He judged a config a
# reader can watch working to be worth more than redacting it. Home network
# only — a work-network address does NOT get this pass.
10[.]1[.]13[.]35

# Same decision, same file: the author's own username and the paths derived
# from it.
/home/[n]ick
C:[\\/]Users[\\/]nick

# A label invented in the WezTerm ssh_domains block, not a resolvable hostname;
# the scanner's topology list matches the word itself. Rename it freely — it
# appears only in the domain name and the tab-title label.
tools[b]ox
